<section class="hc-casestudy">
  <div class="hc-casestudy__inner">
    <div class="hc-casestudy__img-col"><div class="hc-casestudy__img-wrap"><img src="/images/hanita-coatings-window-film-philadelphia-casestudy.jpg" alt="Philadelphia commercial property with Hanita SolarZone XTRM on west-facing curtain wall glass" title="Hanita SolarZone XTRM Philadelphia commercial case study" width="1376" height="768" loading="lazy" class="hc-casestudy__img" /><div class="hc-casestudy__badge"><span class="hc-casestudy__badge-label">Hanita Case Study</span></div></div><div class="hc-casestudy__stat-row"><div class="hc-casestudy__stat"><span class="hc-casestudy__stat-val">81%</span><span class="hc-casestudy__stat-label">Max TSER</span></div><div class="hc-casestudy__stat-div"></div><div class="hc-casestudy__stat"><span class="hc-casestudy__stat-val">West</span><span class="hc-casestudy__stat-label">Facing Curtain Wall</span></div><div class="hc-casestudy__stat-div"></div><div class="hc-casestudy__stat"><span class="hc-casestudy__stat-val">10 yr</span><span class="hc-casestudy__stat-label">Commercial Warranty</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="hc-casestudy__content"><span class="pp-eyebrow">Case Study</span><h2 class="hc-casestudy__title">How a Philadelphia Commercial Property Chose Hanita SolarZone XTRM Over Competing Films</h2><p class="hc-casestudy__lead">A Center City office building with a large west-facing curtain wall needed stronger solar control without changing the facade standard.</p><p class="hc-casestudy__body">The property manager specified Hanita SolarZone XTRM after reviewing technical data from three competing film brands. XTRM's spectrally selective construction delivered the highest TSER while maintaining the near-neutral glass appearance required by building standards.</p><p class="hc-casestudy__body">After installation, peak afternoon cooling load dropped noticeably and occupant complaints about workstation glare were resolved. The building kept its clean exterior look, while the west-facing floors became easier to cool and more comfortable for afternoon work.</p><blockquote class="hc-casestudy__quote"><p>&ldquo;SolarZone XTRM gave us the performance number we needed without making the building look tinted. That combination is why we chose Hanita.&rdquo;</p><footer>Property Manager — Center City Office Building</footer></blockquote><a href="/contact/" class="hc-casestudy__link" aria-label="Ask Window Film Philadelphia about Hanita SolarZone XTRM"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>Ask about SolarZone XTRM<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a></div>
  </div>
</section>

